# The service worker's cache name is a sha256 over the RAW BYTES of the shell
# files, computed once on the machine that builds and again in CI to check the
# stamp shipped. A file rewritten on Windows picks up CRLF, git stores LF, and
# the two sides then hash different bytes for identical code -- the build fails
# with nothing wrong in it. Pin the endings so there is only ever one answer.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
